+What:           /sys/class/power_supply/qcom-battmgr-bat/wireless_care_hold
+Date:           November 2026
+Contact:        dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
+Description:
+                Root-only read/write boolean, exactly 0 or 1, optionally newline.
+                Available with qcom,automatic-bpp-charging. Requests an independent
+                battery hold while retaining normal wireless input. Does not clear
+                the manual charge_behaviour or kernel safety hold. Remains asserted
+                if userspace exits. A successful write records requested policy;
+                inspect wireless_charge_state and measured battery current for
+                physical confirmation. No foreign disabled permission is enabled.
+
+What:           /sys/class/power_supply/qcom-battmgr-bat/wireless_charge_state
+Date:           November 2026
+Contact:        dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
+Description:
+                Read-only key=value diagnostic of automatic input phase, ownership,
+                requested manual/care/safety holds, pending/frozen battery ownership,
+                error stage and service/receiver generations. UNKNOWN or frozen
+                ownership is not a verified off state. Firmware ACKs describe
+                requests, not an applied current limit or measured charging.
+
+What:           /sys/class/power_supply/qcom-battmgr-bat/wireless_voltage_max
+Date:           November 2026
+Contact:        dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
+Description:
+                Read-only qualified normal ADSP maximum voltage sample in microvolts
+                for conservative care policy. Uses a fresh same-response maximum/
+                minimum pair with source, health, temperature and generation guards.
+                Returns an error instead of stale data on unavailable/unsafe input.
+                Does not change battery votes. Not a pack-voltage or Full indicator.
